      environment for your animal companions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Weekly Brushing & Grooming</h2>

    <p>
      Regular brushing is an important part of keeping your cat
      comfortable and maintaining a healthy coat. A gentle weekly
      grooming session helps remove loose fur, reduce shedding,
      prevent tangles, and distribute natural oils throughout the coat.
    </p>

    <p>
      Choose a brush suited to your cat's coat length and texture,
      and gently brush in the direction of hair growth. Pay attention
      to areas where knots can develop, particularly behind the ears,
      beneath the legs, and around the hindquarters.
    </p>

    <p>
      Make grooming a pleasant experience with gentle handling,
      reassurance, praise, and occasional treats. Long-haired cats
      may require daily brushing to prevent mats, while many
      short-haired cats benefit from a weekly routine.
    </p>

    <p>
      Brushing also provides an opportunity to check your cat's skin
      and coat for irritation, unusual lumps, or signs of parasites.
    </p>
  </section>

